WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.380
<b>Sogeking</b>

3
00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.030
We're almost to the exit now.

4
00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.300
Full speed ahead
until we fly outta here!

5
00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.960
What?

6
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:02.560
No way!

7
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.070
You're kidding, right?!

8
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:24.720
All right!

9
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.560
There it is!

10
00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.860
Time to move out, men!

11
00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.160
Let's charge ahead, join
them, and get Franky back!

12
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.130
Yeah!

13
00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.170
Sodom! Gomorrah! Jump!

14
00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.680
Huh?!

15
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.480
Straw Hat!

16
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.060
<b>Sodom and Gomorrah
The Franky Family's
Personal King Bulls</b>

17
00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.520
The entire Franky Family
thanks you for helping us!

18
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:52.020
We'll never forget it!

19
00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.720
Fire the connection cannons!

20
00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.000
Cool!

21
00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.640
Hey, nice job!

22
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.140
Pretty high-grade
bulls you've got there!

23
00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.610
Awesome!

24
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.050
Dammit!

25
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.080
Those stupid bastards!

26
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:18.750
You idiots!

27
00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.190
You gotta be more careful!

28
00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.830
– Thanks for the help!
– Thanks for the help!

29
00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:22.730
Where is it?

30
00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.800
I don't see it anywhere.

31
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.230
Looks like it
drifted a bit, huh?

32
00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.580
Listen I know these sea trains
like the back of my hand.

33
00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.840
I'll find that railway,
no problem!

34
00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.570
Found ya!

35
00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.600
Let's go!

36
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:44.670
Attention!

37
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.610
This train will soon be on the railway.

38
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.410
Once we are, our acceleration
will increase exponentially!

39
00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.740
Find something to hold on to

40
00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.750
so we can keep the
injuries to a minimum.

41
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.450
"A minimum"?

42
00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.450
We'll be injured regardless?

43
00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.300
Listen, you!

44
00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.900
Behave yourself!

45
00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:09.500
Whoa!

46
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.070
That was close, Granny!

47
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.400
A little to the right!

48
00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.340
Meow!

49
00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:14.930
Don't you worry!

50
00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.400
I'll get it next time!

51
00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.770
You'll see!

52
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:19.540
Chimney!

53
00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.980
Gonbe!

54
00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:22.560
No!

55
00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:24.560
I left you with Iceburg!

56
00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.410
Meow! Meow!

57
00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.420
How could this have happened?!

58
00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.760
Get down from there
and come inside!

59
00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.800
You'll be blown away out there!

60
00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.970
We're fine! We're fine!

61
00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.980
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, WHOA!

62
00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.770
Chimney!

63
00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.350
I'm gonna fall!

64
00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.130
Whatever you do, don't let go!

65
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.630
I'm flying!

66
00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.560
Meow!

67
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.160
Wait!

68
00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.700
Hold on a second, okay?

69
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.900
Let me slow down!

70
00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.660
Oh, no!

71
00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:03.230
I forgot!

72
00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.460
No brakes!

73
00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.230
We can't stop!

74
00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.470
Whoa, what the heck?

75
00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.620
Hey, that kind
of looks like fun!

76
00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.710
Look, it's the Straw Hat guy!

77
00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.900
Hi!

78
00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.240
Meow!

79
00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.110
Hurry!

80
00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:20.480
Grab those two and bring them inside!

81
00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:24.450
Once this train hits the railway,
they'll be blown away!

82
00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.580
Right!

83
00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.370
I thought I was a goner!

84
00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.800
You almost were!

85
00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.840
I said "If you
don't come inside,

86
00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.680
you're gonna get blown away!"

87
00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:12.110
Whew!

88
00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.940
That speed was crazy!

89
00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:14.930
Told ya!

90
00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.830
He's right! That was rough!

91
00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.900
Hurt my back.

92
00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:20.800
Hold on a second.

93
00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.740
There're a few more people
in here than there should be.

94
00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:24.190
– Yeah?
– Yeah?

95
00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.120
Who do you mean?

96
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.260
He means you!

97
00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.860
I mean you, too!

98
00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.830
I tried but no matter
what I said or did,

99
00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.700
I couldn't stop you.

100
00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.570
And the enemy that
you'd go through all of this

101
00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:39.570
to rescue your friend from
is the exact same one

102
00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.980
that tried to kill Iceburg.

103
00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:46.480
I've got a word or two of my own
I wanna say to those bastards!

104
00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.150
Yeah!

105
00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.280
You're not the only one!

106
00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.290
We figured that if we snuck
onto the train and followed you,

107
00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.690
we'd be right behind
you when things

108
00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.830
went down with those
no good assassins!

109
00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:56.970
So here we are.

110
00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.740
Seems our hunch was right.

111
00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.740
Let us join you.

112
00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.010
We wanna avenge Iceburg.

113
00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.350
Sounds like we all have a common enemy!

114
00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.920
They're the same ones that
kidnapped our bro Franky!

115
00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:08.120
Yeah, he's right!

116
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.890
No point in playing dumb,
we know exactly who they are!

117
00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.130
Hey, Galley-La!

118
00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:15.040
If anything happens to him, it's gonna be
on your shoulders!

119
00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.050
Can it!

120
00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.850
Iceburg's the one that's
endured the most here!

121
00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.750
Hey!

122
00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.750
What the heck are they talking about?!

123
00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:22.480
Come on!

124
00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.880
There's something you're
not telling us, Paulie!

125
00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.620
Yeah. It's time to come clean.

126
00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.820
Tell us everything.

127
00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.450
We need answers.

128
00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.290
You know who the true culprit is.

129
00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.940
We're not stupid, you know.

130
00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.270
We've got a pretty
good idea who it is.

131
00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.690
You're not gonna surprise us.

132
00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.640
Well, I guess the story

133
00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:42.480
about them disappearing
was too convenient.

134
00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.740
Fine I'll tell you.

135
00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:48.420
The true identities
of those masked men

136
00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:53.290
are Lucci, Kaku, Kalifa,
and Blueno from the bar.

137
00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.790
It was them. They're the ones
who tried to kill Iceburg.

138
00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.560
Are you trying to tell me you
never even thought of them?!

139
00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.860
You said they went
back to their hometowns!

140
00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.600
Come on! You believed that?!

141
00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:06.870
We... We thought it was Michael

142
00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.570
and Hoychael from
the backstreet district!

143
00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:09.440
Right! Right!

144
00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:10.410
Who the hell are they?!

145
00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:10.810
What?

146
00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:11.510
You're kidding!

147
00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.450
You've never heard of them?

148
00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.620
They're pretty famous
in the backstreets!

149
00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:15.820
Right! Right!

150
00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.090
Why would half the foremen
leave in the middle of a crisis!

151
00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.830
Didn't...

152
00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.430
Whew! That really hit the spot!

153
00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.900
Man, I was starving!

154
00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.240
Right.

155
00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.870
So even though we
got in a few fights

156
00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.960
back in town with
both the Franky Family.

157
00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:32.440
And with the
Galley-La shipwrights,

158
00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:35.680
the enemy we're all going
after here is one and the same.

159
00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.940
Now the strongest one,

160
00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:38.510
the toughest out of all of them,

161
00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.470
is definitely that pigeon guy.

162
00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.270
He's mine.

163
00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.240
I'm gonna beat
the crap out of him.

164
00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:44.310
Luffy's right.

165
00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.600
This is a battle to get
back what those four goons

166
00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.600
from the World
Government took from us.

167
00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.860
So we either reach them in time

168
00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.500
or all of this will
be for nothing.

169
00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.800
Granny!

170
00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:55.540
Look!

171
00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.070
It's Aqua Laguna!

172
00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:57.900
Meow!

173
00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:58.660
Oh?

174
00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.520
It's here already?

175
00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.620
Hey, let me take a look!

176
00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:08.330
Oh, no!

177
00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.330
Hey!

178
00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.520
Shouldn't you be in the
engine room right now?

179
00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:13.520
You've gotta find some way
to dodge that gigantic wave!

180
00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:17.900
Rocketman can't be controlled,
remember?

181
00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.500
We can't adjust the
speed, use the brakes,

182
00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.510
or change our course.

183
00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.750
My job ended as soon as I got us up on the
railway.

184
00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:29.040
The train's lined up on the
tracks, running at full speed,

185
00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.920
and there's nothing
anybody can do to stop it.

186
00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:32.890
No.

187
00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.090
Hey!

188
00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.370
If we don't do something,
and fast this train's gonna...

189
00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:44.370
Everybody on this train has the exact same
goal.

190
00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.570
There's no point in fighting separately.

191
00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.280
Yeah.

192
00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:49.680
He's right.

193
00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:54.380
From this point forward,
we fight as one!

194
00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.740
There are two more of my crew on that
other train.

195
00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.010
Once we've caught up to them,

196
00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:01.480
our fighting force
will be even stronger.

197
00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:04.880
Listen up!

198
00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:07.380
We're not gonna let that big wave beat us!

199
00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:10.050
We will achieve our goal!

200
00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.550
Let's go!

201
00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:16.030
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

202
00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.110
All right boys,

203
00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.680
why don't you show me what
you can do about that wave!

204
00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:21.680
You got it!

205
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:22.820
Fire all cannons!

206
00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.990
Blow it to bits!

207
00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.460
Cannons are my specialty!

208
00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:28.660
It's just water!

209
00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.690
Don't be afraid, bros!

210
00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.990
Prepare the cannons!

211
00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.760
Roger!

212
00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.370
– Get a move on!
– Get a move on!

213
00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:49.070
Puru-puru. Puru-puru.

214
00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:52.480
– Ah! The Transponder snail's ringing!
– Ah! The Transponder snail's ringing!

215
00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:56.340
<b>Puffing Tom</b>

216
00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:55.340
Hey guys, it's from Sanji!

217
00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.110
Hey, you there.

218
00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:11.230
<b>Car Five</b>

219
00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.230
Yes, Captain T-Bone!

220
00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.870
How did you get that injury on your arm?

221
00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.270
Huh?

222
00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.540
This?

223
00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.040
I got bitten by a bug earlier
and it bled when I scratched it.

224
00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.380
How awful!

225
00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:24.070
We must staunch the bleeding!

226
00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.370
We'll have to make do with this.

227
00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:30.080
Sir! You don't have to tear
your cape just for me!

228
00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:39.050
"Justice"

229
00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.100
It may be your
arm that's bleeding,

230
00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.920
but when one of
my men is injured,

231
00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.420
it's my heart that hurts the most.

232
00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.360
Captain!

233
00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.420
Thank you!

234
00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:46.890
<b>Captain T-Bone
Marine Headquarters
Hobby: Saving People Motto: 100 Good Deeds A Day</b>

235
00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.340
Let us fill today and every
day forth with good deeds,

236
00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:47.280
so that peace and
kindness shall reign.

237
00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:52.380
– His face is still really scary.
– His face is still really scary.

238
00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:53.940
Captain!

239
00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:56.250
I'll help!

240
00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.790
Oh good, but let me
explain the problem first.

241
00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.760
If there's anything I can do.

242
00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:05.440
Even if it kills me
I will protect you!

243
00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.040
Uh, thanks.

244
00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:11.490
But the problem is with the
officials in car 6 and 7.

245
00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.180
They were completely wiped out.

246
00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:16.890
Not only that, the two criminals detained
in Car 6 are missing.

247
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.940
That's awful!

248
00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.500
We can't tell if the prisoners
escaped on their own,

249
00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:25.030
of if they were helped
by an unknown intruder.

250
00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.500
For heaven's sake, man,
start a rescue operation!

251
00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:30.030
Help the injured and spread
the word to the other cars!

252
00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.560
Yes, sir!

253
00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.150
Nami!

254
00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:34.500
Nami, can you hear me?

255
00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:35.080
Yeah!

256
00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.450
What's going on, Sanji?

257
00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:38.200
I've got some bad news.

258
00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:40.350
Things have gotten complicated.

259
00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.820
What do you mean?

260
00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.420
Hey, wait a sec
what was that noise?

261
00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:48.380
Is someone there with you or something?

262
00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.990
It's nothing just some dumb ass.

263
00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.090
Huh? Say what?

264
00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:55.630
Sanji!

265
00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.330
What's that noise?!

266
00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.160
It sounds like a bunch

267
00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.130
of screaming-are you
okay over there?

268
00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.860
What d'you mean by "dumb ass"?

269
00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.830
Sorry, dumb asses, actually.

270
00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:09.560
Demi Cannon!

271
00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:18.180
– Leave it to us!
– Leave it to us!

272
00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:19.810
Not even making a dent.

273
00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.220
I shoulda figured.

274
00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.820
You think those puny things are gonna
work?

275
00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:24.920
Everybody, step back!

276
00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.700
Let the Franky Family's
Special Cannon do its stuff!

277
00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.670
Target Aqua Laguna!

278
00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.160
Go!

279
00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.470
Super Scrap Cannon, fire!

280
00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.520
Fire again!

281
00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.080
Don't let up!

282
00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.190
Bring more cannonballs!

283
00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:55.230
Got it!

284
00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.200
Aim at the center!

285
00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.580
Focus on one spot!

286
00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:00.230
Focus pocus,
give it all you got!

287
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.630
Yeah, good luck with that.

288
00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.520
By the way, the
tracks do rise up a bit

289
00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:07.620
but not enough to
get us over that wave.

290
00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:10.320
Rocket Man has done
pretty well out here so far.

291
00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:12.660
But if we get hit, we're finished.

292
00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:15.500
Does that mean
we're all gonna die?!

293
00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.530
No guarantees!

294
00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:20.170
I warned you, now didn't I?

295
00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:23.630
I don't wanna die!

296
00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:26.720
I see.

297
00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.540
They still have Robin.

298
00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.680
It sounds like things are
pretty lively on your end, too.

299
00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.410
Hey listen, Sanji.

300
00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:38.780
I need to tell you why Robin's doing all
this.

301
00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:42.450
And also why everyone's
screaming, for that matter.

302
00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.820
Shut up!

303
00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.620
So, like I was just saying.

304
00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.560
We found out why
Robin's with CP9.

305
00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:51.740
We're out here
trying to follow her,

306
00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.150
but things are kind
of crazy right now.

307
00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:55.450
It's a long story.

308
00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.670
We're all gonna die!

309
00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.520
But I don't wanna die!

310
00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:02.360
Me either!

311
00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.840
If you have time to cry, keep firing!

312
00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.810
We'll find a way out!

313
00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.100
Hey, Luffy.

314
00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:11.970
Yeah.

315
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.610
I know what you're thinking.

316
00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.340
That wave's asking for it, huh?

317
00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:26.250
C'mon!

318
00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.650
Keep those cannon's firing!

319
00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.720
What're you guys
planning on doing?

320
00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.530
Same thing as you.

321
00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.770
Watch.

322
00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.900
Hey, how much is a hundred and eight times
two?

323
00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.660
Two hundred and sixteen.

324
00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.470
Two hundred sixteen, huh?

325
00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.400
That's too long.

326
00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.170
Can't we round up or something?

327
00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:04.500
Fine make it 300, then.

328
00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.370
I don't get it. What do they
think they're doing?

329
00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.140
If cannons don't work, what
good are swords are gonna do?

330
00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.450
Well, they did say we should keep
fighting, though.

331
00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:13.260
Stop yapping and back them up!

332
00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.430
Roger!

333
00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.270
Okay!

334
00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:19.300
Ready?

335
00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.810
Uh-huh.

336
00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:23.280
Now Gum-Gum...

337
00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.740
Three Hundred Caliber...

338
00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:33.500
– We... We made it!
– We... We made it!

339
00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:45.350
Take that, Aqua Laguna!

340
00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.840
I thought we were gonna die!

341
00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.240
Hey! Hey, Nami are you okay?

342
00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:21.750
Yeah, I-I think so.

343
00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:24.210
We survived after all, huh?

344
00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:26.160
You pirates know how to party!

345
00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:28.190
Keep up the good work!

346
00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:30.360
They're even stronger than Aqua Laguna!

347
00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.830
If we were enemies,
I'd be scared right now,

348
00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.970
but since we're
friends, I'm happy!

349
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.340
– Go Straw Hat!
– Go Straw Hat!

350
00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:38.970
We'd all be dead right now if not for
them.

351
00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.470
Lucky that little trick worked.

352
00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:43.440
Let's not get ahead of ourselves,
everybody!

353
00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.450
We're not through the storm yet!

354
00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.520
– Yes, ma'am!
– Yes, ma'am!

355
00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:50.110
I'm not afraid of
anything, anymore!

356
00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.280
Wow, that was really fun!

357
00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:58.980
I knew you were strong, but that was
something else!

358
00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:00.180
Are you an alien or something,

359
00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:03.160
'cause that was totally
out of this world!

360
00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:05.100
Oops.

361
00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:06.830
Sorry 'bout that.

362
00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.000
Luffy, c'mere a sec.

363
00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:09.200
Huh?

364
00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:16.040
Sanji wants to talk.

365
00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:18.050
That you, Luffy?

366
00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:20.350
Yep, it's me!

367
00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.380
What's up?

368
00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:22.980
You save Robin?

369
00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.720
No, sorry.

370
00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.560
Afraid I'm still working on that one.

371
00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:28.520
Nami just told me
why Robin surrendered

372
00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:28.950
and all of that stuff.

373
00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.690
So yeah I know what's going on.

374
00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:34.290
I see.

375
00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.920
That's good.

376
00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:39.660
Well anyway,
you know what's next.

377
00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.290
Go ahead. Give 'em hell, Sanji.

378
00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.230
He'll die if he fights them now!

379
00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:46.100
If wants to stand a chance,
he's gotta wait on us!

380
00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.420
Hey, Cook, can you hear me?

381
00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.630
Some of the guys on that train

382
00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:51.140
are really tough,
you shouldn't...

383
00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:52.000
Zoro!

384
00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.330
It's fine.

385
00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.690
If it was you, would you wait?

386
00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:58.890
If you were on that train
right now instead of him and

387
00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.860
I told you that Robin sacrificed
herself to protect us.

388
00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:05.600
Would you just sit
there and do nothing?

389
00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:10.870
No use trying to stop him.

390
00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.630
Read me like a book.

391
00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:14.200
But thanks, Moss Head.

392
00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.660
I never knew that you cared about me so
much.

393
00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.280
I hope they kill you!

394
00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.380
Anyway, that settles it.

395
00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:24.480
I was willing to fight for Robin even
before I knew the truth.

396
00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.650
But now that you told
me how she really feels.

397
00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.610
I wouldn't stop,
even if you begged me.

398
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.130
Why'd you break
it, you bastard?!

399
00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.010
I wanted to talk to
Straw Hat, too, damn it!

400
00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.640
Huh?

401
00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.240
Deal with it.

402
00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:41.950
No point in griping at me now.

403
00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.420
What, was I supposed
to interrupt you

404
00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:44.600
while you were talking?

405
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:45.670
That's just rude!

406
00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:48.700
You're rude anyway.

407
00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.910
I hope he's okay on his own.

408
00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:53.560
Granny, hurry!

409
00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.430
Make the train go faster!

410
00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:56.650
Faster?

411
00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:57.840
Yeah!

412
00:20:57.870 --> 00:21:01.510
More like zoom, y'know?

413
00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:04.370
Oh, don't you worry!

414
00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.780
This baby is already
going way faster

415
00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:09.310
than it was ever supposed to!

416
00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.680
In fact, we're going so fast,

417
00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.820
we can't even stop anymore!

418
00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:19.420
<b>Puffing Tom</b>

419
00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:23.170
So much stuff has happened since I left.

420
00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:25.670
It almost doesn't seem real.

421
00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.440
In a way, Robin's in the same boat you
are.

422
00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:29.810
Never found out
about what happened

423
00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:33.880
with the Merry or
your fight with Luffy.

424
00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:36.900
It makes me ashamed to think it

425
00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.970
but while we were busy
fighting amongst ourselves.

426
00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.210
Robin surrendered to the
government

427
00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:46.710
so the six of us could be safe.

428
00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:48.810
That includes you.

429
00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:51.950
Oh, man!

430
00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:54.850
That's such a sad story!

431
00:21:58.320 --> 00:21:59.860
Why are you crying?

432
00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.470
I'm not crying, you are!

433
00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:05.840
Damn it!

434
00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:06.850
Now I'm all torn up!

435
00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:09.440
I always thought Robin
was some evil monster,

436
00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:11.670
but it turns out
she's got a soft side!

437
00:22:11.710 --> 00:22:14.270
What if I'm confused
about other stuff, too?!

438
00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.240
How am I supposed to go on?

439
00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.810
I'm not gonna stand here in
the rain when Robin's so close.

440
00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:22.650
I gotta save her
before it's too late.

441
00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:23.750
Sweet.

442
00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:26.320
Once again, I'm Franky,
leader of the Franky Family.

443
00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:28.690
You 'n me'll make a
good team, Eyebrows Bro.

444
00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:29.820
I won't go into the details,

445
00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:32.420
but I've got a pretty good
reason to keep Robin away

446
00:22:32.470 --> 00:22:34.370
from those
government chumps, too!

447
00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:35.910
Besides, you really
touched my heart

448
00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:37.540
with that story of yours.

449
00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:40.310
Hey, Long-Nose,
let's do this thing!

450
00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:46.350
No, I'm... I'm not coming.

451
00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:49.640
This doesn't have anything to do with me
anymore.

452
00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:51.610
You're about to make
yourselves personal enemies

453
00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:52.950
of the World Government.

454
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:55.620
I don't want to be any part of that.

455
00:22:55.650 --> 00:22:59.590
Besides, Luffy and the rest of the crew
are coming.

456
00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:02.190
After I humiliated
myself in front of them.

457
00:23:02.220 --> 00:23:04.090
I just can't pretend like
nothing ever happened

458
00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:05.860
and laugh it off.

459
00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:12.130
I still feel bad for
Robin but I'm sorry.

460
00:23:12.130 --> 00:23:14.500
It's not my job to save her now.

461
00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:17.030
I am not a part of Luffy's crew!

462
00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:23.340
See ya.

463
00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:28.390
"See ya?" There's
no place to go!

464
00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:29.150
Come on!

465
00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:31.620
You guys can talk this over, bro!

466
00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:33.750
Forget it.

467
00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:36.950
Just leave him.

468
00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:40.490
You are both stubborn as hell.

469
00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:43.720
Check every corner!

470
00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:45.830
They gotta be here somewhere!

471
00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:47.470
What?!

472
00:23:47.540 --> 00:23:50.650
This is just terrible!

473
00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:52.290
<b>Car Seven Interior</b>

474
00:23:50.830 --> 00:23:52.290
We'll have to make do with this.

475
00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:56.040
The train's in a lot
of trouble right now!

476
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:59.130
<b>Car Four
(Kitchen)</b>

477
00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:56.810
Wanze!

478
00:23:56.850 --> 00:23:57.880
We need your help!

479
00:23:57.920 --> 00:23:59.720
Shut up, stupid!

480
00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:01.680
Your face is in trouble!

481
00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:04.130
<b>Car Three</b>

482
00:24:04.190 --> 00:24:06.920
Nero! The criminals
made an escape!

483
00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:08.090
Hm?

484
00:24:10.190 --> 00:24:12.000
How's it going over there?

485
00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:14.100
Have you noticed
anything strange?

486
00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:24.340
They're right here!

487
00:24:24.370 --> 00:24:25.940
Dammit, they found us!

488
00:24:25.970 --> 00:24:27.540
Metallic Star!

489
00:24:34.980 --> 00:24:36.580
– Who the hell are you?!
– Who the hell are you?!

490
00:24:43.490 --> 00:24:45.560
Your friend told me everything.

491
00:24:45.590 --> 00:24:46.390
I understand that you are here

492
00:24:46.400 --> 00:24:49.110
to rescue a certain
mademoiselle.

493
00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:52.760
That alone is reason enough for me to join
your cause.

494
00:24:53.110 --> 00:24:56.280
My weapons are at your disposal.

495
00:25:02.320 --> 00:25:06.120
My name is Sniper King.
